Dear Mrs Rainho,

Thank you for your reply and for confirming that my N463 application has be=
en referred to the case lawyer.

I would like to clarify that my request for urgent judicial consideration i=
s made in the context of my status as a disabled and medically vulnerable li=
tigant. I am currently experiencing severe and escalating health deteriorati=
on, and any delay in judicial consideration increases the risk to my health.

=20

As the underlying claim directly concerns HMCTS=E2=80=99s handling of my particip=
ation measures and reasonable adjustments, I respectfully remind the Court t=
hat its fully engaged duties under the Equality Act 2010 (ss.20=E2=80=9321), the P=
ublic Sector Equality Duty (s.149), and the overriding objective concerning =
vulnerable litigants apply to the handling of this N463 request.

=20

I would be grateful if this could be brought to the immediate attention of =
the case lawyer so that my application can be considered with the urgency re=
quired in light of my medical position and statutory protections.

=20

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

=20

=20

From: "Administrative Court Office, Case Progression" <administrativecourto=
ffice.caseprogression@justice.gov.uk>
Date: Tuesday, December 2, 2025 at 8:05=E2=80=AFAM
To: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>
Subject: RE: AC-2025-LON-004293 =E2=80=93 Urgent Judicial Consideration Required =
(Disabled/Vulnerable Litigant)

=20

Dear Nadia,

I acknowledge receipt of both emails.

The N463 was filed yesterday with the turnaround of 72h. I confirm that it =
wad referred to the case lawyer yesterday and will be dealt with in due cour=
se.

Kind regards,

=20

=20

Mrs Erica Rainho=20

Case progression Officer=20

Administrative Court Office | King=E2=80=99s Bench Division I HMCTS I Royal Court=
s of Justice I Strand, London I WC2A 2 LL | Phone: 020 7947 6655 | Web: www.=
gov.uk/hmcts

=20

