=20

From: Nadia <nadia@rosekross.com>=20
Sent: 02 December 2025 14:21
To: Administrative Court Office, Case Progression <administrativecourtoffic=
e.caseprogression@justice.gov.uk>
Subject: AC-2025-LON-004293 =E2=80=93 Urgent Judicial Consideration Required (Dis=
abled/Vulnerable Litigant)
Importance: High

=20

Dear Case Progression Team,

=20

I am writing urgently regarding my Judicial Review claim AC-2025-LON-004293=
. The claim was issued on 1 December 2025, and the Defendants (HMCTS and MoJ=
) were served on 2 December 2025. An urgent consideration request (N463) was=
 included with the bundle.

=20

For clarity, I am a disabled and medically vulnerable litigant, and the sub=
ject matter of this claim directly concerns HMCTS=E2=80=99s handling of my partici=
pation measures and reasonable adjustments. I am currently experiencing seve=
re and escalating health deterioration linked to the same issues raised in t=
he claim. Any delay in urgent judicial consideration places me at further cl=
inical risk.

=20

As you will be aware, the Court has fully engaged duties under:
Equality Act 2010, ss.20=E2=80=9321, to ensure reasonable adjustments for disable=
d court users;
the Public Sector Equality Duty, s.149, requiring due regard to eliminating=
 discrimination and advancing equality for disabled persons;
and the overriding objective, including the requirement to ensure that vuln=
erable litigants can participate effectively and without avoidable harm.
=20

Given these duties, I respectfully request confirmation that my application=
 for urgent consideration has been placed before a judge without delay. I wo=
uld also be grateful to know whether any further information is required fro=
m me at this stage.

=20

Thank you for your assistance and understanding in what is, for me, a medic=
ally fragile and time-critical situation.

=20

Kind regards,

Nadia Zahmoul

Email: nadia@rosekross.com

=20

